    {
      "section": 4,
      "kind": "context_only",
      "source_line": 376,
      "snippets": [
        {
          "source_line": 386,
          "tex": "We introduce the following notation:\nWe set $\\Lambda^\\natural$ to be the quotient of $\\Lambda$ by its additive\nsubgroup generated by the commutators (i.e., the elements of the form\n$ab-ba$, $a, b \\in \\Lambda$). Note that $\\Lambda^\\natural$ is not a ring."
        },
        {
          "source_line": 407,
          "tex": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-trace}\nThe {\\it trace} of the endomorphism $a$ is the sum of the diagonal entries of\na matrix representing it. This defines an additive map $\\text{Tr} :\n\\text{End}_\\Lambda(\\Lambda^{\\oplus m}) \\to \\Lambda^\\natural$.\n\\end{definition}"
        }
      ],
      "stage_a_readiness": "no_active_candidates",
      "stage_a_source_context_reviewed": true,
      "stage_a_source_context_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14",
      "stage_a_candidate_ids": [],
      "stage_a_held_candidate_ids": [],
      "stage_a_source_context_heading": "Traces",
      "stage_a_source_context_summary": "Finite ring Λ of order prime to p, commutator quotient Λ^natural and trace; coefficient assumptions §4-local only."
    },
    {
      "section": 5,
      "kind": "context_only",
      "source_line": 446,
      "snippets": [
        {
          "source_line": 449,
          "tex": "\\noindent\nWith this definition of the trace, let us now discuss another issue with the\nformula as stated. Let $C$ be a smooth projective curve over $k$. Then there is\na correspondence between finite locally constant sheaves $\\mathcal{F}$ on\n$C_\\etale$ whose stalks are isomorphic to\n${(\\mathbf{Z}/\\ell^n\\mathbf{Z})}^{\\oplus m}$ on the one hand, and continuous\nrepresentations $\\rho : \\pi_1 (C, \\bar c) \\to\n\\text{GL}_m(\\mathbf{Z}/\\ell^n\\mathbf{Z}))$ (for some fixed choice of $\\bar c$)\non the other hand. We denote $\\mathcal{F}_\\rho$ the sheaf corresponding to\n$\\rho$. Then $H^2 (C_{\\bar k}, \\mathcal{F}_\\rho)$ is the group of coinvariants\nfor the action of $\\rho(\\pi_1 (C, \\bar c))$ on\n${(\\mathbf{Z}/\\ell^n\\mathbf{Z})}^{\\oplus m}$, and there is a short exact\nsequence\n$$\n0 \\longrightarrow \\pi_1 (C_{\\bar k}, \\bar c) \\longrightarrow \\pi_1 (C, \\bar c)\n\\longrightarrow G_k \\longrightarrow 0.\n$$\nFor instance, let $\\mathbf{Z} = \\mathbf{Z} \\sigma$ act on\n$\\mathbf{Z}/\\ell^2\\mathbf{Z}$ via $\\sigma(x) = (1+\\ell) x$. The coinvariants\nare $(\\mathbf{Z}/\\ell^2\\mathbf{Z})_{\\sigma} = \\mathbf{Z}/\\ell\\mathbf{Z}$, which\nis not a flat $\\mathbf{Z}/\\ell^2\\mathbf{Z}$-module. Hence we cannot take the\ntrace of some action on $H^2(C_{\\bar k}, \\mathcal{F}_\\rho)$, at least not in\nthe sense of the previous section."
        }
      ],
      "stage_a_readiness": "no_active_candidates",
      "stage_a_source_context_reviewed": true,
      "stage_a_source_context_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14",
      "stage_a_candidate_ids": [],
      "stage_a_held_candidate_ids": [],
      "stage_a_source_context_heading": "Why derived categories?",
      "stage_a_source_context_summary": "Source intervals and definitions examined in chronological order; prior theorem hypotheses not carried forward."
    },
